    <article>
        <header class="mt-8 sm:mt-10">
            <p class="font-mono text-[11px] tracking-[0.16em] uppercase" style="color:#57D29A">No 10 · Guide</p>
            <h1 class="mt-4 font-display text-[30px] leading-[1.14] font-extrabold tracking-[-0.01em] text-pretty sm:text-[38px] md:text-[44px] md:leading-[1.1]">Five Habits For A More Focused Working Week</h1>
            <div class="flex flex-col gap-2 text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-muted mt-4">
    <p>By <a href="https://habitkit.app/about" rel="author" class="font-semibold text-silver hover:text-accent focus-ring">Sebastian Röhl</a>, creator of HabitKit</p>
    <p class="flex flex-wrap gap-x-3 gap-y-1">
        <span>4 min read</span>
        <span>Published <time datetime="2024-10-29">Oct 2024</time></span>
                    <span>Updated <time datetime="2026-09-14">Sep 2026</time></span>
                    </p>
</div>
        </header>

        <div class="help-body guide-lead mt-8 sm:mt-9"><p>Notifications, competing tasks and an unclear stopping point can make a working day feel scattered. A few repeatable routines can give it some structure.</p>
<p>Here are five ideas to try, with a way to record each in HabitKit. They are practical suggestions, not a tested programme or a promise of higher productivity. Pick one that addresses a problem in your own week before adding the others.</p>
</div>

        <details class="rounded-xl border border-white/10 bg-panel px-4 py-3 mt-6">
        <summary class="cursor-pointer text-[14px] font-semibold text-silver focus-ring">On this page</summary>
        <nav aria-label="Article contents" class="mt-3">
            <ul class="flex list-none flex-col gap-1">
                                    <li><a href="#choose-one-habit-for-this-week" class="block rounded py-2 text-[14px] leading-relaxed text-muted hover:text-accent focus-ring">Choose One Habit For This Week</a></li>
